-- title:
--   Level automorphisms permute node places and Igusa ends
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime and $M'$ a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lying over $q$ in the sense that $q$ is a non-unit of $A$. The field `fieldBar q M'` is the base change to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (coefficientwise, inside Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$) of the function field of the modular curve $X_H$ of level $q^2M'$, where $H =$ `levelH q M'` is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$; `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` is the base change to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the field generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the expansions $j(d\tau)$ for $d \mid M'$, and `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` is the subfield of Laurent series over $\kappa$ generated by the expansions of $j$ and of $j(M'\tau)$. For $\zeta$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (an element of `Idx q`) and $\gamma \in \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$, `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` is the chosen $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-automorphism of `fieldBar q M'` realising the action of $\gamma$ normalised by $\zeta$ (the automorphism selected by the predicate `IsLevelAutBar`, which compares, under any embedding of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ into $\mathbb{C}$ sending $\zeta$ to $e^{2\pi i/q}$, the image of a quotient of two modular forms with integral $q$-expansions to the quotient of their slashes by `conjElem q γ`; the identity if no such automorphism exists).
--
--   The standing data are as follows. A finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` is given, with the hypothesis `hW` that $W$ consists exactly of the supersingular places `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)` (those places which are rational, are affine geometric places, and whose value at the geometric $j$-coordinate lies in the supersingular $j$-set `ssJSet q`). The hypothesis `hle` states that `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` is contained in `fieldBar q M'`. Next, $R_0$ is a constant reduction of $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'`: a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ together with a surjective residue homomorphism onto the target whose kernel is the maximal ideal, agreeing with $A$ on constants, compatible with the residue map of $A$, admitting constant rescalings with nonzero residue, and with a map on places preserving degrees and pushing forward principal divisors to the order divisors of residues. The compatibility hypothesis `hR₀` states that for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose coefficientwise image lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that element lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over the residue field of $A$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$. Finally $s \in W$ is a chosen supersingular place and $wd$ a natural number (the width).
--
--   A ground field $k_0$, an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$, is given with an element $\pi_0 \in k_0$ lying in $A$ (`hπ`), and the hypotheses (`hdvr`, `hunif`, `hhens`, `hres`) that the contraction $A \cap k_0$ is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, is henselian, and has algebraically closed residue field, together with `hκ`: every element of $A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0$ lying in $A$.
--
--   Auxiliary prime and root data: a prime $\ell \ge 3$ with $\ell \ne q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$, an element $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ which is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity, and an element $\varpi_t \in k_0$ lying in $A$ such that $\varpi_t^{q^2-1} = q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$ (`hϖt`).
--
--   Tower data: a type $\iota$, a family $K$ of intermediate fields of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/k_0$, each finite over $k_0$ (`hKfin`), valuation subrings $A_n$ of $K_n$ cutting out $A$ (`hAn`), an index $n_0$ with $K_{n_0} \le K_n$ for all $n$ (`hn₀`), and cofinality `hKcof`: every finite subset of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is contained in the image of some $K_n$. Also an element $\pi_t \in A$ with $\pi_t^{q^2-1} = q$ (`hπt`, `hπA`) and the tameness hypothesis `htame`: every element of the inertia subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ on which the tame character of $A$ with respect to $\pi_t$ (the residue of $\tau\pi_t/\pi_t$) is trivial fixes $K_{n_0}$ pointwise.
--
--   Bottom-layer data: an intermediate field $K_b$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/k_0$ with $K_b = \bot$, a valuation subring $A_b$ of $K_b$ cutting out $A$ (`hAb`), and a nonzero $\varpi_b \in A_b$ generating the maximal ideal of $A_b$.
--
--   The assertion is the following, `fieldBar q M'` being regarded as a $k_0$-algebra through $k_0 \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}} \to$ `fieldBar q M'`. Let $F_0$ be an intermediate field of `fieldBar q M'` over $k_0$ satisfying the four level-field conditions: (F1) $f \in F_0$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $f$ lies in $k_0$; (F2) the subfield generated over $k_0$ by the constants $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ together with $F_0$ is all of `fieldBar q M'`; (F3) $F_0$ is stable under `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` for every $\zeta$ and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; (F4) for every finite extension $K'$ of $k_0$ inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, every family $c_1,\dots,c_m \in \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ linearly independent over $K'$ and every family $a_1,\dots,a_m$ in the compositum of $k_0(K')$ and $F_0$ with $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$, all $a_i$ vanish.
--
--   Let further $W_0$ be a valuation subring of $F_0$, let $B$ be a subring of `fieldBar q M'` carrying an $A_b$-algebra structure, and let there be given: `hjR`, that the image of the expansion $j$ lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$; `hjs`, that its $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of the place $s$; `hJK`, that the expansion of $j(q\tau)$ lies in `fieldBar q M'`; an element $a_0 \in k_0$ lying in $A$ whose residue satisfies $\overline{a_0}^{\,q} = s(\overline{j})$ (`hpin`, where $s(\cdot)$ denotes evaluation at $s$); and a finite set `nodes` of subrings of $F_0$. Assume the long hypothesis block, whose conjuncts are, in order: (W1) $W_0$ traces $A$ on $k_0$; (W2) $W_0$ is a discrete valuation ring; (W3) $\pi_0$ lies in $W_0$ and generates its maximal ideal; (W4) a reduction-compatibility clause at $s$, requiring for each $g$ in the full modular function field of level $M'$ whose image lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and which is regular wherever $j$ is (at every place $P$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}\,j$ implies $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}\,g$) and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, that the image of $g$ lies in $F_0$ and in $W_0$ and is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $W_0$ to every constant $c \in k_0 \cap A$ whose $A$-residue equals the value at $s$ of that $R_0$-residue; (W5) $W_0$ is invariant under the level automorphisms; and a block about $B$ and `nodes` whose conjuncts (summarised here) are: the $A_b$-algebra structure on $B$ is the one induced by the inclusions; $B$ is contained in the compositum of $k_0(K_b)$ and $F_0$, and every element of that compositum is a fraction of two elements of $B$; $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A_b$, and $B/\varpi_b B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; every element of $B$ lies in $F_0$ and in $W_0$; the image of $\varpi_b$ is prime in $B$; $W_0$ consists exactly of the fractions $g/h$ with $g,h \in B$ and $\varpi_b \nmid h$; the image of $j$ lies in $B$, and $B$ is stable under the level automorphisms; there is an element of $B \cap F_0$ which lies outside every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ that traces $A$ on $k_0$, has $\pi_0$ in its maximal ideal, contains $j$ and has $j$ with residue not annihilated by the reduction of any monic polynomial over $k_0$ with $A$-integral coefficients; for each supersingular place $s' \ne s$ in $W$ there is likewise an element of $B \cap F_0$ lying outside every valuation subring of $F_0$ satisfying the reduction-compatibility clause at $s'$; a Drinfeld-model clause, asserting that for every $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$-algebra structure on the residue field $\kappa$ of $A$ making [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) a domain, and every $\zeta$, there are a subgroup $C_s$ of the $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$ with $|C_s| = wd$ and a ring homomorphism $\rho$ from $B$ to [`DrinfeldCurve.quotField q κ Cs`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCoveringW2.html#L32) with kernel the ideal generated by the image of $\varpi_b$, reducing $A_b$ through the residue map of $A$, with every element of the target a fraction of values of $\rho$, with image exactly the elements lying in the image of the coordinate ring, and equivariant for the $h$-action of $(\mathrm{red}_q\gamma,1)$ against `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹` whenever $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and that pair lies in `hSubgroup q`; and a nodes clause asserting that `nodes` has $q+1$ elements, that there is a subring $B_c$ of $F_0$ generated by the constants from $k_0 \cap A$ together with a finite set which is contained in every node and of which every node is the localisation at its own units, that the level automorphisms permute `nodes` and act transitively on it, that distinct nodes are separated by a function which is a non-unit in one and a unit in the other, that every valuation subring of $F_0$ tracing $A$ on $k_0$ and satisfying the reduction-compatibility clause at $s$ either contains $B$ or dominates one of the nodes, and, for each node $O$, a package of per-node data: $O \subseteq W_0$, $O$ is local and Noetherian, traces $A$ on $k_0$ and has all residues coming from $k_0 \cap A$; there exist $E_0 \ge 1$ with $\pi_0^{E_0} = \varpi_t^{\,wd}\,v$ for a unit $v$ of $A \cap k_0$, elements $c_x, c_y \in O$ with $c_xc_y = \pi_0^{E_0}u$ for a unit $u$ of $O$, and a ring isomorphism of the adic completion of $O$ with the crossing model $\widehat{A \cap k_0}[[U,V]]/(UV - \pi_0^{E_0})$ which matches constants and carries $c_x$, $c_y$ to unit multiples of $U$, $V$, with $c_y$ in the maximal ideal of $W_0$ and $c_x$ a unit of $W_0$; the function $j(q\tau) - a_0$ lies in $F_0$ and in $O$ and is carried to a unit multiple of $V^e$ for some $e \ge 1$; there is an Igusa-side end, a valuation subring $W_x$ of $F_0$ containing $O$, tracing $A$ on $k_0$, a discrete valuation ring uniformised by $\pi_0$, containing an element whose residue is transcendental in the sense that a polynomial over $k_0$ with $A$-integral coefficients taking a value in the maximal ideal at it has all coefficients in the maximal ideal, with $c_x$ in the maximal ideal and $c_y$ a unit, with a clause relating membership in its maximal ideal to vanishing of $R_0$-residues and, at $s$, to membership in $O$ and congruence to the matching constant, and excluding every other node; and there is a subring $B_x$ of $F_0$ contained in $B \cap O$, consisting of functions regular wherever $j$ is, of which $O$ is the localisation at its units, with fraction field $F_0$, generated by the constants from $k_0 \cap A$ together with a finite set, and containing an element lying outside every valuation subring $V$ as in the clause above which omits some element of $O$.
--
--   Under these hypotheses the following holds. Let $F_{ss}$ be a field that is an algebra over the residue field of $A$, let $R$ be a regular prolongation of $A$ from `fieldBar q M'` to $F_{ss}$ (a valuation subring with surjective residue map onto $F_{ss}$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal, agreeing with $A$ on constants, compatible with the residue map of $A$ and admitting constant rescalings with nonzero residue) whose ring of integers cuts out $W_0$ on $F_0$. Let $N$ be a finite set of places of $F_{ss}$ over the residue field of $A$ and $\mathcal{O}_{(\cdot)}$ an assignment of subrings of $F_0$ to places such that $\mathcal{O}$ maps $N$ into `nodes`, hits every node, and is injective on $N$; let $S$ assign to each place a set of places of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, so that for $nd \in N$ a place $P$ lies in $S(nd)$ exactly when $P$ dominates $\mathcal{O}_{nd}$, that is, every element of $\mathcal{O}_{nd}$ lies in the valuation subring of $P$ and every non-unit $f$ of $\mathcal{O}_{nd}$ has $P$-value in the maximal ideal of $A$. Assume the centre conditions: for each $nd \in N$ the $R$-residues of elements of $\mathcal{O}_{nd}$ lie in the valuation subring of $nd$, the non-units of $\mathcal{O}_{nd}$ have $R$-residue in its maximal ideal, and $nd$ is the unique place of $F_{ss}$ with these two properties. Assume finally the Igusa-end data: fields $F_{I,x}$, algebras over the residue field of $A$, regular prolongations $R_x$ of $A$ from `fieldBar q M'` to $F_{I,x}$, and valuation subrings $W_x$ of $F_0$, such that for $nd \in N$ the ring of integers of $R_{nd}$ cuts out $W_{nd}$ on $F_0$, $\mathcal{O}_{nd} \subseteq W_{nd}$, $\pi_0$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_{nd}$, and there is an element $c_y^O \in \mathcal{O}_{nd}$ which is a unit of $W_{nd}$, whose $R$-residue is $0$, and which pins $W_{nd}$ canonically: every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ containing $\mathcal{O}_{nd}$, with $\pi_0$ in its maximal ideal and $c_y^O$ a unit, contains $W_{nd}$.
--
--   Then two statements hold. First, for every $\zeta' \in$ `Idx q` and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ there is a map $\tau_N$ on the places of $F_{ss}$ over the residue field of $A$ such that for every $nd \in N$: $\tau_N(nd) \in N$; for every place $P$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ one has $(\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta'\,\gamma) \cdot P \in S(nd)$ if and only if $P \in S(\tau_N(nd))$; and the preimage of the ring of integers of $R_{nd}$ under `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` equals the ring of integers of $R_{\tau_N(nd)}$. Second, for every $\tau$ in the subgroup of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-automorphisms of `fieldBar q M'` generated by the automorphisms `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\zeta' \in$ `Idx q` and $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, and every proof that $\tau$ preserves the ring of integers of $R$, one has for every $nd \in N$: the place $R.\mathrm{resAut}(\tau) \cdot nd$, obtained by transporting $nd$ along the automorphism of $F_{ss}$ over the residue field of $A$ induced by $\tau$, again lies in $N$, and $\{P : \tau^{-1}\cdot P \in S(nd)\} = S(R.\mathrm{resAut}(\tau) \cdot nd)$.
--
--   This is the equivariance step in the analysis of the semistable fibre at $q$ of the modular curve $X_H$ of level $q^2M'$ with $H$ the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$: once the supersingular fibre has been presented by $q+1$ node local rings together with their place-sets, centres and Igusa-side ends, the level automorphisms attached to $\Gamma_0(M')$ are shown to permute these data, both the sets of places dominating a node and the prolongations cutting out the Igusa-side ends. It is stated for every prime $q$ and with a free width parameter $wd$, and is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.klevel_nodeCore_nodeCharts_hasseGerm_nodeCentre_of_affineChart_poles_hasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_of_eq_two_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.klevel_nodeCore_nodeCharts_hasseGerm_nodeCentre_of_affineChart_poles_hasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_of_eq_two_of_dvd), which reads the width without an extra factor $2$.
